    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "The no3/po4 fields are per unit volume (mol m-3), so converting them to the requested micromoles per kilogram at 1025 kg/m3 and comparing them with WOA23's per-mass observations is a units step this fragment governs.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Convert `no3`/`po4` to µmol kg-1 using µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ; the question's constant ρ = 1025 kg m-3 is followed, and the answer must state this density assumption (the fragment would use in-situ density below the surface).",
        "Ratios of two tracers converted with the same ρ need no conversion; a constant-density conversion leaves N:P unchanged, but do not label a mol m-3 × 1e3 value as µmol kg-1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The cell-by-cell N:P ratios, regression and model-vs-WOA23 differences exist only where both fields have data, so a single common mask must be built and applied to every field in the comparison (with WOA23's mask used only where WOA23 itself is involved).",
      "status": "not_applicable",
      "not_applicable_reason": "no shared-mask model–observation difference or multi-model ranking is requested; each source's metrics are computed on its own valid cells."
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "The \"percentage of water volume\" and the 200–1000 m layer selection require volcello as tracer-cell volume (with layer thickness recovered from volcello/areacello, and deptho for the sea floor) rather than counting cells.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use `volcello` for the 200–1000 m layer volume and every volume weight, not `lev_bnds` differences; `cell_thickness_like` returns volcello/areacello, and 14% of GFDL-ESM4 cells differ by more than 1%.",
        "`deptho` is model bathymetry, not external topography; use the field's own valid cells/`deptho` to decide ocean points."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "Global and basin statistics of a volume fraction must be volume-weighted over all ocean cells and integrals must use every grid point with no subsampling, which is what the requested volumetric percentages are.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Volume-weight all means (layer, basin, ratio of means) as Σ x·`volcello` / Σ `volcello`, with weights masked to the same valid cells; a plain `mean()` is wrong.",
        "Report the cell-by-cell N:P mean (`compute_ratio`) and the ratio of volume-weighted means separately; the question's equal-cell-weight OLS also differs from the fragment's area-weighting advice, so follow the question and state both choices."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "The 1971–2000 source fields are averages of monthly means, and the headline diagnostic (cell-by-cell N:P) is nonlinear, so ratios formed from these monthly values differ from the ratio of the averaged nitrate and phosphate and that must be handled/stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Form the 1971–2000 climatology as the plain mean of each calendar month across years; day weights do not enter a monthly climatology, and equal-weighting all months would be a period mean, not a climatology.",
        "N:P is nonlinear: f(monthly mean) ≠ monthly mean of f; N:P from climatological mean `no3`/`po4` is the diagnostic of the mean state (like-for-like with WOA) — state that order."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "The Pacific/Atlantic/Indian summaries depend on which basin partition is used (WOA23 basin mask, marginal seas folded in, Southern and Arctic excluded) and the fragment requires that partition to be stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use the WOA23 mask with `select_basin(..., include_marginal_seas=True)`; state that this is WOA labelling, not the OMIP 10-region mask, and that Southern/Arctic are separate and excluded.",
        "Use `depth_dependent=False` (surface labels through the water column) for named-ocean 200–1000 m basin means."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bgc-model-structure-comparison",
      "severity": "info",
      "path": "datasets/bgc-model-structure-comparison.md",
      "sha256": "4ef3e4ab0b9741f6ab5d15f88cfbdf8b7366c82b093ce99e26f1707a2a788e54",
      "reason": "The three models differ in stoichiometry (CESM2 variable C:P, GFDL fixed N:P per plankton type, MPI fixed Redfield), DOM pools and N2 fixation, which shapes the cross-model N:P differences and the low-N:P denitrification signal independently of physics.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Interpret cross-model N:P spread via structure: GFDL has fixed N:P per plankton type, MPI prescribed Redfield, CESM2 variable C:P; \"not detailed in paper\" does not mean absent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "CMIP6 land and below-sea-floor cells carry the 1e20 missing value, and any read path that skips CF masking would turn those into huge numbers that silently dominate the sums, means and regressions computed here.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Decode 1e20 fill to NaN; build each field's mask from itself and compute N:P only where both `no3` and `po4` are valid, masking volume weights to those cells; near-1e20 output is an unmasked fill.",
        "Use `compute_exceedance_fraction` for the 14–18 and <12 volume shares; it excludes missing cells from numerator and denominator and returns the volume behind the percentage."
      ]
    }
